Article 4 (Persons Eligible for Scholarships)
Scholarships shall be paid to nationals of firm convictions and upright conduct who fall under any of the following: <Amended on August 8, 1973; May 8, 1979; and July 2, 2019.>
1. A person with talent who has difficulty receiving education at a middle school or higher-level school for economic reasons;
2. A person with outstanding talent who receives education at a domestic or foreign university or graduate school in an academic field or technology essential to the State;
3. A student enrolled in an agriculture-related department of a university who wishes to engage in actual agricultural management after graduation;
4. A person with particularly outstanding talent who conducts research in Korea or abroad in an academic or technological field considered to make a substantial contribution to the State or human culture: Provided, That researchers dispatched by the Government shall be excluded.
